From 65819a93a49216b3750aa3cb038228c389d82c20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ed Schofield <ed@aicharmers.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:38:26 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] drm/amd/display: Recover the iMac companion after resume

Resume detection can run before the companion tile is ready. With
recovery disabled, the first ordinary S3 resume lost DP-1.

Before restoring and freeing the cached display state, record the mapped
connectors if the saved primary is active at 2560x2880. Allow an inactive
companion. Scaled single-stream modes keep the base driver's emulated
companion. Check the saved CRTC mode: imac5K_using_5K records mode history
and can outlive the stream.

Keep the cached-state restore warning, and queue a worker only if the
return value reports success. Try at most three times: 500 ms after
resume, then 1000 and 2000 ms after each failure.

The primary-only case is important. An earlier revision required both
tiles to be active and lost the companion's native identity after
primary-only S3. A userspace probe, a 60-second wait and blank/wake did
not bring it back, but an explicit ordinary detection did, without
enabling the companion.

On each attempt, cancel if the primary is inactive or either connector
is forced. Detect the companion, then restore it on the route userspace
currently uses. A code review showed that restoring the saved route
would miss route changes or removal. Without a companion route,
publish the sink and leave routing to userspace. Repeat the checks after
detection, which drops the modeset locks.

Skip work if a validated sink is already in the active stream or is
already published without a route. Keep a successfully acquired sink
across restore failures; a valid-looking sink left by failed detection
still needs detection again.

Send at most one hotplug event when the worker finishes. A change to the
published sink still needs an event after late cancellation or if
userspace restores the route first. An unresolved final attempt sends
an event too. A sink acquired during resume and later disabled by
userspace needs no extra event.

Return restore failures as errno. Send hotplug events outside hpd_lock,
and synchronously cancel the worker before releasing either connector
reference. Keep ordinary HPD and DPMS handling unchanged.

A successful atomic commit does not prove the link trained. GPU reset
and the boot timeout fallback still need separate validation.

Signed-off-by: Ed Schofield <ed@aicharmers.com>
